 the shape of a maple leaf is characterized by its lobed nature, with 3 to 5 pointed lobes, with the base of the leaf being attached to the stem. The shape of a maple leaf is also characterized by its pointed tip, with a long petiole, also known as a stem. The leaf is typically 3-5 inches (7.6-13 cm) in length and 1.5-3 inches (3.8-7.6 cm) in width. The color of the leaf is typically green, with lighter colors on the bottom and darker colors on the top, giving it a characteristic "bluish-greens" color.
